From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cargo: build faer and pulp without "nightly" on riscv64

Every non-ARM target enables pulp's and faer's "nightly" features.
faer's "nightly" turns on faer-entity/gemm/gemm-common "nightly", which
all end up enabling pulp/nightly. On riscv64, pulp 0.18.22 then does

    #[cfg(all(feature = "nightly", target_arch = "riscv64"))]
    pub use core::arch::riscv64::*;

without adding #![feature(riscv_ext_intrinsics)], so the crate fails
to compile on the nightly toolchain:

    error[E0658]: use of unstable library feature 'riscv_ext_intrinsics'
      --> pulp-0.18.22/src/core_arch/mod.rs:24:13

pulp has no riscv64 SIMD paths for "nightly" to switch on (its
re-export is never used on riscv64), so on riscv64 build faer and pulp
without "nightly", as Cargo.toml already does for ARM. faer keeps the
same "std", "rayon", "serde", "rand", "npy" features. The dependency
graph is unchanged, so Cargo.lock still resolves with --locked; on
x86_64 the feature set is identical to before.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against azmyrajab/polars_ols]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 Cargo.toml | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -40,7 +40,12 @@ ndarray-linalg = {version = "*"}
 faer = { version = "*" }  # don't allow nightly for ARM due to issues with NEON support
 faer-ext = { version = "*", features = ["ndarray"] }

-[target.'cfg(not(target_arch = "arm"))'.dependencies]
+[target.'cfg(target_arch = "riscv64")'.dependencies]
+pulp = { version = "0.18.22" }  # pulp's "nightly" re-exports core::arch::riscv64 without enabling riscv_ext_intrinsics
+faer = { version = "*", features = ["std", "rayon", "serde", "rand", "npy"] }
+faer-ext = { version = "*", features = ["ndarray"] }
+
+[target.'cfg(not(any(target_arch = "arm", target_arch = "riscv64")))'.dependencies]
 pulp = { version = "0.18.22", features = ["nightly"] }
 faer = { version = "*", features = ["std", "rayon", "serde", "rand", "npy", "nightly"] }
 faer-ext = { version = "*", features = ["ndarray"] }
--
